# Requests for the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
# Click "Send Request" above a request line to run it.
#
# Start the server first, in a terminal:
#
#   npm run dev                      local, reads ENCRYPTION_KEY from .env
#   docker compose up --build        or in Docker, same port
#
# All data below is synthetic. This file holds no key and needs none:
# the key stays in .env, which only the server reads.
#
# Timings assume the default MOCK_AI_DELAY_MS=2000 and MOCK_AI_FAILURE_RATE=0.
# REST Client shows the status and the elapsed time at the top of the
# response tab.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@inquiryUrl = {{baseUrl}}/secure-inquiry


### 1. Health
# Expected: 200  {"status":"ok"}  in a few milliseconds.

GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### 2. Valid inquiry with an email, a card number and an SSN
# Expected: 200  {"answer":"Generated Answer"}  in about 2 seconds
# (the mock AI's delay).
# The AI receives the redacted text only. The audit record holds
#   "redactedMessage": "Hi, I am Ana. Email <REDACTED: EMAIL>, card
#                       <REDACTED: CREDIT_CARD>, SSN <REDACTED: SSN>."
# and the original message encrypted (see "Audit records" below).

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "http-user-1",
  "message": "Hi, I am Ana. Email ana.demo@example.test, card 4111 1111 1111 1111, SSN 123-45-6789."
}


### 3. Valid inquiry without sensitive data
# Expected: 200  {"answer":"Generated Answer"}  in about 2 seconds.
# Nothing to redact: the audit record's redactedMessage equals the message.
# The original is still stored encrypted.

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "http-user-1",
  "message": "What are your opening hours on Saturday?"
}


### 4. Invalid: message is missing
# Expected: 400 in a few milliseconds.
#   {"error":"Invalid request","details":["message is required"]}
# Requests 4 to 8 never reach the AI and leave no audit record.

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "http-user-1"
}


### 5. Invalid: blank userId, wrong type and an extra property
# Expected: 400 with every problem at once, and no submitted value repeated:
#   {"error":"Invalid request","details":["userId must not be blank",
#    "message must be a string","Only userId and message are allowed"]}

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "",
  "message": 42,
  "role": "admin"
}


### 6. Invalid: malformed JSON
# Expected: 400  {"error":"Malformed JSON"}
# The body below is cut off on purpose, so the editor marks it as an error.

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "http-user-1", "message":


### 7. Invalid: wrong content type
# Expected: 415  {"error":"Content-Type must be application/json"}

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: text/plain

My SSN is 123-45-6789


### 8. Unknown path
# Expected: 404  {"error":"Not Found"}

GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist


########################################################################
# Circuit breaker: four requests, sent one after another
########################################################################
#
# The mock's settings are read when the server starts, so making it fail
# needs a restart. Stop the server (Ctrl+C) and start it with the mock
# failing every time after 2,000 ms:
#
#   Local:    MOCK_AI_FAILURE_RATE=1 MOCK_AI_DELAY_MS=2000 npm run dev
#   Docker:   docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.failing-ai.yaml up -d
#
# Variables given on the command line win over the ones in .env, so .env
# is not edited.
#
# Then send 9a, 9b, 9c and 9d in order, waiting for each response before
# the next. Do not restart the server or save a source file in between
# (npm run dev restarts on save): the breaker lives in memory, and a new
# process starts closed. Send 9d within 30 seconds of 9c; after that the
# circuit lets one probe through and 9d takes 2 seconds again.
#
# Expected:
#   9a  503  {"answer":"Service Busy"}  about 2 s    first failure
#   9b  503  {"answer":"Service Busy"}  about 2 s    second failure
#   9c  503  {"answer":"Service Busy"}  about 2 s    third failure, opens the circuit
#   9d  503  {"answer":"Service Busy"}  a few ms     circuit open, AI not called
#
# All four are audited: outcomes ai_failure, ai_failure, ai_failure,
# circuit_open.

### 9a. Breaker, request 1 of 4 (503 in about 2 s)

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "http-user-2",
  "message": "Breaker request 1. My SSN is 123-45-6789"
}


### 9b. Breaker, request 2 of 4 (503 in about 2 s)

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "http-user-2",
  "message": "Breaker request 2. My SSN is 123-45-6789"
}


### 9c. Breaker, request 3 of 4 (503 in about 2 s, opens the circuit)

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "http-user-2",
  "message": "Breaker request 3. My SSN is 123-45-6789"
}


### 9d. Breaker, request 4 of 4 (503 in a few milliseconds)

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "http-user-2",
  "message": "Breaker request 4. My SSN is 123-45-6789"
}


########################################################################
# Restore normal configuration
########################################################################
#
# Stop the failing server and start it again without the two variables:
#
#   Local:    Ctrl+C, then  npm run dev
#   Docker:   docker compose up -d
#
# The new process has a closed circuit because it restarted, not because
# it recovered. Recovery inside one process is shown by  npm run demo.

### 10. After the restart
# Expected: 200  {"answer":"Generated Answer"}  in about 2 seconds.

POST {{inquiryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "http-user-3",
  "message": "Is the service back?"
}


########################################################################
# Audit records
########################################################################
#
# Every request that passed validation (2, 3, 9a to 9d, 10) added one
# record, in order, to the JSON audit file. There is no HTTP endpoint for
# it; open the file:
#
#   Local:    data/audit-log.json  (open it in the editor; the path can be
#             changed with AUDIT_LOG_PATH)
#   Docker:   docker compose exec api cat /app/data/audit-log.json
#
# In each record:
#   userId, timestamp, outcome   readable
#   redactedMessage              readable, with <REDACTED: ...> tokens
#   originalMessage              ciphertext, iv and tag (AES-256-GCM)
#
# Searching the file for "4111 1111", 123-45-6789 or ana.demo finds nothing.
# The file is ignored by Git. Deleting it while the server is stopped
# starts a new, empty log.
